 "intro": "In Aquitania, near Burdigala (Bordeaux) or Agen on the Garonne, 107 BC. The Tigurini, allies of the Cimbri, have raided southern Gaul. You are the consul Lucius Cassius Longinus, pursuing them. The sources are brief.",
 "debrief": "Caesar, Livy’s summary and Orosius report that Cassius was ambushed and killed by the Tigurini, perhaps under the young Divico, along with his legate Piso, and that the survivors under Gaius Popillius had to give hostages and half their baggage and pass under the yoke. Popillius was tried for the terms. Caesar later avenged the defeat at the Arar in 58 BC. The exact place is uncertain. The other choices are what-ifs.",
